# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Narration audio — 599 MB that ships to production and is never read there.
#
# The Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .` with no data/ exclusion, so every tracked byte under
# backend/ landed in every Railway image: 688 MB, of which the running app reads about
# 1.9 MB (the ten book_audio manifests, the two *_universe.json, whale_registry.json and
# the two Learn content JSONs). The clips themselves are served to users from Supabase
# Storage — book-media (10), journey-media (207), money-moves-media (16) — never from disk.
#
# ⚠️ KEEP everything else under data/book_audio/. `book_audio_service.py:31,45` globs
# *.manifest.json AT IMPORT, so losing those empties BOOK_AUDIO_CATALOG and
# GET /api/v1/learn/books/audio answers `temporarily_unavailable` for every user — and it
# degrades at logger.warning, so nothing surfaces the failure. The *.readalong.json are the
# read-along timings, whose only regeneration path is a forced-alignment pass over the very
# audio excluded here. That is why these patterns name the audio extensions rather than the
# directory.
#
# Consequence to know: a regeneration script run on Railway (`generate_*_audio.py`) skips
# clips whose .m4a exists locally, and inside the container none now do. Re-run those from
# a local checkout, or let the seeders fall back to the bucket URL as they already do.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/book_audio/*.m4a
data/book_audio/*.m4a.orig
data/book_audio/orig/
data/book_audio/orig_speed/
data/journey_audio/
data/money_moves_audio/
data/journey_audio_gemini_bak/
data/money_moves_audio_gemini_bak/
data/money_moves_audio_clone/
data/voice_samples/
data/voice_clone/
